From a28976871604f3a414915c2ba976c0ac1b0c67d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junjie Cao <junjie.cao@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:46:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pps: intel_tio: fix use-after-free on MMIO mapping
 failure

On MMIO mapping failure, pps_tio_probe() frees pdata before reading
pdata->sh_res_base. Both pdata and pps_tio are allocated with
devm_kzalloc(), so direct kfree() is also invalid.

Remove the manual frees and return the mapping error while pdata is
still valid. Leave resource cleanup to devres when probe fails.

Signed-off-by: Junjie Cao <junjie.cao@intel.com>
---
 drivers/pps/intel_pps_tio/pps_tio_plat.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pps/intel_pps_tio/pps_tio_plat.c b/drivers/pps/intel_pps_tio/pps_tio_plat.c
index 14b1a4aa610e..54a754b0fe6e 100644
--- a/drivers/pps/intel_pps_tio/pps_tio_plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pps/intel_pps_tio/pps_tio_plat.c
@@ -409,11 +409,8 @@ static int pps_tio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	pdata->sh_res_base = devm_ioremap_resource(&pdev->dev, res);
-	if (IS_ERR(pdata->sh_res_base)) {
-		kfree(pdata);
-		kfree(pps_tio);
+	if (IS_ERR(pdata->sh_res_base))
 		return PTR_ERR(pdata->sh_res_base);
-	}
 
 	ret = ida_alloc(&tio_ida, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-- 
2.34.1

